WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.800
- I got this present, and it reads, "To Evan
Carmichael, merry Christmas and happy New

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.730
Year, "with lots of love from Believe Nation."

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:47.870
- [Female] Do you want to watch it?

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:53.140
- These are my top 10 videos.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.680
- You going to watch it?

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.739
- I'm a little scared.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.600
- He's a former venture capitalist, radio
host, YouTube personality and entrepreneur.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.070
- He sold his first company at 19.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.900
- He set two world records.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.240
- He aimed to help while being an entrepreneur.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:16.140
- He's Evan Carmichael and here are his top
10 rules for success.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.030
- When I was growing up in grade two, grade
three, grade four, I used to have a lot of

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.180
nervous ticks.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.380
Some of them were really embarrassing.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.850
I used to blink a lot constantly.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:31.149
I used to do this with my neck and then have
to adjust with my shoulder.

00:01:31.149 --> 00:01:35.270
When I was walking I used to always have to
step on the lines or completely avoid the

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.830
lines in the sidewalk.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:41.090
One of the most embarrassing one was I used
to always try to kick my own butt where I

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:47.710
would always have the, I'd have to push my
leg up and I wouldn't be happy until the heel

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:48.710
hit my butt.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.090
And I have to do that a couple times before
I can move on with the rest of my day.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.850
I was also getting into a lot of fights at
my school.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.930
So seeing this, my parents were really worried.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.329
And they took me to go see a child psychologist.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:00.400
I didn't know she was a psychologist.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.119
My parents just said I was going to go play
games with somebody and we had some games

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:07.939
together and she showed me these ink blots
and told me, "What do you see in these pictures?"

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:09.910
And she asked me a bunch of questions.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.820
The immediate recommendation was that I switch
schools right away.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.160
And so in grade five I transferred to a new
school called Crescent and ended up staying

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.690
there from grade five all the way to graduating
high school.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:21.710
And the ticks got better.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:24.019
For the most part they went away completely.

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:28.330
To this day I still have a few minor ones
where if I'm thinking or if I'm stressed or

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.459
if I'm tired, you can see my ears move.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:32.340
But other than that, they're gone.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.060
What it really made me think about was the
importance of your environment.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.170
See, your environment is either something
that builds you up, that lifts your spirits,

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.769
that helps you go chase your dreams.

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:43.110
Or it's something that squashes you down.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.350
That makes you shrink.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.480
That makes you accept a lesser life.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.490
So think about the people that you surround
yourself with, think about the TV shows you're

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:55.260
watching and the media that you're consuming
and the place that you go to work.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.449
Does your environment build you up or squash
you down?

00:02:58.449 --> 00:03:03.269
Changing my environment had a dramatic impact
on the quality of my life and the contribution

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:05.590
to my success as an entrepreneur.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:08.009
Achieving yours can have the same impact for
you.

00:03:08.009 --> 00:03:10.360
- Add more value.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.070
If you want to be able to charge what you're
worth, if you want to be able to build a successful

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.329
company, you need to add a ton of value.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:22.280
The amount of money that you make will be
directly related to how much value you're

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.440
providing for your customers.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.750
How much you're helping them out.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:29.170
It's a pretty simple equation.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.490
Executing it is difficult.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.480
But the concept is simple to understand.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:41.310
If you want to make more money add more value
and stop competing on price.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.760
When you compete on price alone it's a loser's
game.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.370
You're not going to bring on ideal clients.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.859
You're constantly going to be struggling to
get by.

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:52.380
You're not going to be able to hire great
people for your team.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.269
You have to stop competing on price, start
adding more value and you're going to love

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.269
your business more.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:03:59.540
You're going to have more fun.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:02.900
You're going to attract much better clients.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.010
You want to work with people who understand
the value you provide and not just cater to

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:13.370
the guys who have no budget who are barely
paying you a tiny profit for what you're doing.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.310
I believe everybody has one word that they
stand for and when you figure out what that

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.540
one word is, your life and your business will
change.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:25.930
And it's not just for marketing, it's not
just how you promote yourself, but it's who

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:30.910
your surround yourself with, the team that
you attract yourself to, the products and

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.160
service that you launch.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:39.880
When I encompanied and embraced believe as
my one word, my business started to take off.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.290
My videos started doing insanely better.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.500
I started attracting the right people into
my team.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:49.220
I started launching products that made sense
for people and people really embraced.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:55.090
And so I'm a huge believer in it and I'm going
to give you a quick method to how to figure

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.090
out your one word.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.150
The first step is you think about what makes
you happy.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.150
What are the things that make you come alive?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.850
What are the things that you love doing?

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.160
And just, don't even think about what your
one word is yet.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.760
Just think about all the things that you love
doing, things you could do all day long, and

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.280
things that fill your life with joy.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.650
Write those things down.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.260
And this isn't just a business thing, this
is you personally.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:18.540
'Cause you want to make this personal for
your business to be successful.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.970
The second this is that look at what connects
them.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.920
What are all the things that connect those
things that make you happy?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.250
What's the connective tissue and try to figure
out is there one word that can bring all those

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.250
things together?

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:36.100
So think about what your favorite movie is,
your favorite book, your favorite, your best

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.430
friend growing up, what you love about your
parents, you know, what businesses you've

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.210
been attracted to, the hobbies that you love
doing.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.210
What connects them all together?

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.460
For me it's believe.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:51.510
You know, I love Seabiscuit as a movie which
is about this underdog horse.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:56.140
And underdog jockey and underdog trainer and
underdog owner and how they all work together

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.530
to then win a whole bunch of races.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:04.160
The songs that I listen to are always the
uplifting, believe, kind of positive ones.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.620
Those are the ones that I gravitate towards.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:09.130
What I love about my parents is that they
always believed in me and told me that I was

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.730
a Carmichael and I could do anything that
I wanted.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:16.670
Even if they didn't give me the ideas on how
to start a business, they always believed

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:22.510
that whatever I did I would be successful
at and taught me to believe in myself.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:25.370
And so it's real important.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:30.520
And so all of those things that I've done
across my life have been about believe and

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:36.730
when I encompass that it allowed me to start
living my life on purpose, with direction,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.071
instead of just being reacting to it.

00:06:39.071 --> 00:06:41.110
The thing is that every industry is competitive.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.280
Right, every industry is competitive.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.290
And the key is you got to be you.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.350
The key thing that's going to make you stand
out from everybody else is you.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.670
I'm trying to cross the street as I'm saying
this.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.190
That's the differentiator.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.400
That's your market advantage.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.090
And so you got to figure out, yes, you can
model success.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.830
Yes, you can look at people who are big in
the beauty industry and look at how they rose

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.330
and those are great examples.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.790
You've got to take what worked for them and
then make it your own.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:09.770
You've got to find a way to make this your
business and people will be attracted to your

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:10.770
personality.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:12.570
Not everybody, but a certain group of people.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.480
And what I found the best way to do it is
to combine your passions.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.850
So if you love beauty, that's amazing, that's
awesome, what else do you love?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.600
And how can you mix those two things?

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.530
So for example, say you love dancing.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.780
Right, you love dancing, that's your passion
besides beauty.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.970
Be the beauty person for dancers.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:29.970
Right?

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.100
The next time doing a photo shoot, the next
time they're getting ready for a performance,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:37.590
the next time they're out there getting to
a movie, I almost got run over by that guy.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.590
Holy cow.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.140
They're going to call you, right?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:46.490
You're making videos, you're writing the blog
post, you're Tweeting about makeup and beauty

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.490
and dancing.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.490
And so that's the key, that's how you do it.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:53.950
A couple examples that I've used before in
the video, one, if you like being a photographer,

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.240
photographers are super competitive, too.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.430
But say you love bowling.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:59.970
Then you can be the photographer for bowlers.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:04.450
And you're going to be the default person
they go to because they need people to be

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:07.510
able to take pictures and they want somebody
who's passionate about bowling.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.830
If you love dancing, they need people who
can do makeup but they want people who are

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.790
passionate about dancing as well and you can
speak both languages.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:14.790
That's the key.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.870
I got a buddy of mine, I've used an example
before, named Steve, who's a financial planner.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.290
A financial planner?

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.590
How many financial planners are there out
there?

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.590
Tons.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.590
But he has a passion for hockey.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:28.570
He loves hockey, he obsesses over it, he watches
it, you know, as much as he can.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:29.980
Watches the same replay 20 times.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.300
He can just watch hockey day in and day out.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.180
He became the financial planner for hockey
players.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:39.130
And so when he's talking to hockey players,
now, he can speak their language, he can talk

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:42.229
about hockey, he can talk about investments
and he's one of them.

00:08:42.229 --> 00:08:43.229
Right?

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:46.399
A lot of these hockey players, you know, the
goal in financial planning is to target the

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:47.399
high net worth individuals, right?

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:48.440
The people who have a lot of money.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.360
Those are the people you want to work with.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:53.280
And so he's able to do that by combining his
passions.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.630
And so make it your own, right?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:59.709
Find a way to be able to tie whatever other
passions you have into the beauty business

00:08:59.709 --> 00:09:00.930
and that's how you're going to stand out.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.850
I want to see more of this, I want to see
your passion, I want to see your personality,

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.640
your character, what you believe in.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.620
All of that, it's got to be real, it's got
to be you, it's got to be human and that connection

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:14.650
to you and everything that you stand for and
believe in is what's going to make me want

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.339
to come to you as opposed to everybody else.

00:09:17.339 --> 00:09:18.480
That's how you stand out.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.620
One of the most important lessons that I've
learned in business, and I guess in life,

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.490
is you need to follow your flow.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:30.010
And sometimes there are external pressures
that force you into following your flow.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.210
You may get a big meaty opportunity.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.120
You may get a partnership.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:39.920
You may get a big customer that kind of is
a huge, big opportunity for your business.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:43.430
And sometimes follow your flow, I find, comes
from internal reasons.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.430
Internal pressures.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:47.870
Maybe you wake up one day and you really want
to go try something out.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:52.370
Or you're on a walk or you're in the shower
and a new thing comes to your mind.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:59.300
And I found that by following my flow, by
following that idea, it's always in my best

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.300
interest.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.520
One, because probably magic is going to happen.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:06.770
If magic is going to happen it's going to
come from a source of inspiration.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.700
Not just being, you know, doing your day to
day to day to day.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.630
And two, I didn't want to live with regret,
you know?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.740
Didn't want to have this big list of to-do's.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:19.590
This big list of ideas that just builds and
builds and builds and this Evernote file that

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.380
just keeps growing and I never actually take
action on stuff, right.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:27.260
You have an idea, you want to try something,
go and take action on it.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:33.260
So yesterday, because this relates to my book,
yesterday I had a full day planned.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.300
Monday is my busy day.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.910
I record these on Tuesdays.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.750
Mondays are my busiest day of the week.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:44.370
And I had a full day planned and it all exploded
on me.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.020
From an external source.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:47.520
From 50 Cent.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:51.910
So I made a video and 50 Cent saw it and he
called it, "Good shit."

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:56.110
And he posted on his Facebook page and he
posted it to his Twitter account.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:57.570
He posted a blog about it.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:04.279
He kind of went crazy promoting this and as
a result the traffic exploded on my video,

00:11:04.279 --> 00:11:06.110
comments were coming out of everywhere.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.339
People were Tweeting me, they're signed up
for my newsletter.

00:11:08.339 --> 00:11:10.230
They're engaging with the video.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.550
It was just insane.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:16.180
And I had a choice of hey, I could either
go with this, right, or I could just do all

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.660
the work that I had planned for the day.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.660
And I chose to go with it.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.350
On top of it, it was pretty cool, right?

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:25.399
50 Cent likes my stuff and is sharing it and
I spent a good amount of time just with my

00:11:25.399 --> 00:11:27.630
team just having fun in the moment.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:31.600
Looking at the numbers, seeing where it was
being shared, it's kind of a big celebration

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:32.860
and a win for everybody on the team.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.990
So we're all kind of super pumped and excited.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:39.501
And I spent the day responding to everybody
and as a result, got nothing done that I was

00:11:39.501 --> 00:11:41.550
supposed to get done for the day.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:42.650
Hello Believe Nation.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:46.420
I talked a lot about, on this channel, how
when you first start at something you're going

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:47.420
to suck at it, right?

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.380
Any new skill that you kind of pick up, you're
going to suck whether it's learning a language,

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:55.080
picking up a new sport, picking up a new skill,
learning the video games, trying to understand

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:58.870
marketing or accounting, whatever it is you're
trying to understand, you will suck at the

00:11:58.870 --> 00:11:59.870
start.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:03.240
And the story I've told a couple of times
on these videos is look back on my channel,

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.310
look back on old videos and see the progress,
right?

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:11.080
2500 videos later you can see how I've grown
and I've gotten better and I sucked at the

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.080
start.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.399
And hopefully sucked a little bit less now.

00:12:15.399 --> 00:12:23.020
But one thing that struck me as I was watching
through my channel was the Entspresso series.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:28.930
I started that a couple months ago and the
first one that I did was of Dame Dash.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.810
And it was a selfish project for me because
I wanted something in the morning to kind

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.899
of get me excited, get me inspired, make me
think bigger.

00:12:35.899 --> 00:12:39.560
But when I started it I didn't have it all
planned out and I think this is something

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:46.640
that's really critical for a lot of you entrepreneurs
is you want to not over plan and expect to

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:47.810
suck at the start.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.170
And it's okay because you're going to get
better and better and better and better.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:54.750
- I remember when I had my first company,
I really struggled at the beginning.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:58.550
I was making 300 bucks a month, not enough
to survive.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:04.770
Almost gave up repeatedly and was willing
to try anything.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:08.660
I felt like I had tried everything and nothing
was working out.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:13.330
I had a great product and I couldn't understand
why this was so hard because the books I've

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:18.890
read and the websites I've visited, and the
shows I watched, everything seemed to be so

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:19.890
easy.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.089
Like, follow these eight steps and you'll
be successful.

00:13:21.089 --> 00:13:26.430
Well I've followed those eight steps a million
times and I wasn't successful.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:31.550
And one of the big breakthroughs for me came
when I realized that I wasn't the first guy

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:32.970
to try to do this before.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:37.260
My first company was a software company and
I had no background in software before.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:41.339
Apart from using a computer, but I wasn't
a software designer.

00:13:41.339 --> 00:13:45.680
And the breakthrough moment came when I did
realize that I'm not the first guy to try

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:50.779
to sell software before and I went and I modeled
some of the largest and most successful software

00:13:50.779 --> 00:13:52.050
companies in the world.

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:54.930
And one in particular was Microsoft.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:14:00.170
And again, I don't care how Bill Gates makes
money now but how did you go from nothing,

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:02.760
from that idea, to getting his first customer.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:06.510
What did he do, what did he say, what were
his options, what was his mindset?

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.790
Who did he need to connect with?

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:13.649
And I took those strategies and applied them
to my business and I finally started to see

00:14:13.649 --> 00:14:16.930
results.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.310
For him it was through partnerships.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:23.580
So he made partnerships, he had software,
he partnered with hardware companies.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:27.740
His big deal came with IBM, it was a seven
million dollar deal, that first one with IBM

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.850
that really put the company on the map but
before that he still made partnerships with

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.300
other hardware companies.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.500
And they sold their products as a bundle.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:40.480
And so I applied that strategy and within
the first month I closed my first partnership

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.120
deal and I made 13 and a half thousand dollars.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:48.990
Now that may not seem like a lot of money
to you, 13K, but to me I'm making 300 bucks

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.740
a month, this was like eureka.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.990
Oh my God, I struck it rich.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.500
This is amazing.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.730
Somebody actually believes in what I'm doing.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:02.110
I'm seeing some positive momentum finally
after all this failure and struggling.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.300
And I just kept copying that again, and I
applied it again and again and again and closed

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.440
more partnerships and more partnerships and
continued to grow my business and eventually

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:12.540
I got acquired by someone who was a potential
partner.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:16.200
They loved us so much that they wanted to
buy my business.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.890
And I wish I had discovered it earlier.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:21.220
I wish I'd discovered the strategy so much
earlier.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.690
Because I almost shut down.

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:26.790
Like, I almost quit my business and thought
maybe I should listen to my friends and go

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.960
back and get a job.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:34.750
And I'm so grateful that I didn't but I came
close many times to having to do that.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.029
And so if you're struggling with your business
right now, if you don't have a lot of experience

00:15:38.029 --> 00:15:42.700
in the field and it's a first time thing for
you, you can't get this thing off the ground,

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:43.700
model success.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:48.250
Find someone who has done it, who's had success
in your field.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:52.090
Look at the cosmetic alliance company, see
how they did it, learn from their mistakes

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:55.850
so you don't have to make all the mistakes
yourself.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.300
And you crunch down your learning curve so
instead of it taking you years and years and

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:04.970
years to achieve success you can do it a lot
faster because you're modeling things that

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:05.970
work.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:06.970
That's the test.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:10.149
You know, when you are excited by something,
when you are passionate about something, when

00:16:10.149 --> 00:16:14.290
you're willing to set an alarm for something
and then wake up even before that alarm goes

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:19.440
off, that tells you that you're on the right
path because too many people try to plan it

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.440
all out, right.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.790
Try to make it make sense up here in your
head, right?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.350
It's got to make total logical sense before
I launch.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:28.570
And your assumptions are always going to be
wrong.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:32.579
And it's never going to work out like you
think it will and you spend so much time planning

00:16:32.579 --> 00:16:34.860
that you don't spend any time doing.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:38.630
And what you need to do is follow your passion
even when it sounds crazy.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:41.580
You know, I don't know how this business is
going to work out.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:45.360
I don't know if it's going to be with videos,
I don't know if it's going to be through an

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:49.400
